There's nothing particularly special about this ascension, except that
I have finally ascended one of every class :)  Checking my local
record book reveals a fairly poor ascension rate (4.6%), so I've got a
long way to go to reach Marvin, but thanks again to the folk of rgrn
and #nethack for helping me get from 0 ascensions in 12 years to 16 in
9 months (14 local, 2 NAO; 3 wizards, 2 barbs, and 1 each of the
others).

The story of Hi the Arbalester, a ranger in the service of Venus

In a pretty typical early run, the ranger conquered Sokoban followed
by the Mines.  Hi found both levitation and conflict rings on his
journey, which made the Castle a breeze even without a tonal
instrument.  Hi captured the wand of wishing and picked a few choice
pieces of gear, including his beloved T-shirt and a suit of grey
dragon scale mail.  Perseus had left behind a shield of reflection,
which allowed Hi to ditch the amulet of reflection he had found in
Sokoban.  The dungeon was replete with other useful items such as
gauntlets of power, speed boots, and magic markers (3 death drops and
1 shop), so to avoid pestering Venus, Hi wished for the famed athame.
After a recharge, Hi wished for a better helmet than his dwarvish
iron, and trotted off to complete the Quest.

In the chest kept by his leader, Hi found yet another wand of wishing,
which he carefully tucked away and ended up never using.  Scorpius was
no match for a ranger levitating above the mystic word of power, and
the Longbow of Diana became another inventory adornment.  Having
gathered up a multitude of gold, Hi then donated repeatedly to priests
and enchanted his armor until he felt "safe".  To ensure his clothing
could not be harmed, Hi also genocided the scary blue disenchanting
beasts.

Turning to Gehennom, Hi proceeded to wreak havoc among the domains of
the demon princes.  Asmodeus he bribed away, and Baalzebub he turned
to stone.  Juiblex stood helpless before Magicbane, and Orcus also
became a statue before Hi shattered the ornament to obtain the
powerful wand of death.  Descending further, Hi found the dungeon to
be shallower than he would have expected (VS at DL46).  Hi marked the
strange vibrating square with captured jewels and headed back up the
mazes to deal with the towers he had found.  The wizard's tower was
easily cleansed except for an annoying titan.  Vlad's tower provided
an amulet of life saving, which did its duty admirably when Hi
accidentally fell down a hole while wielding the corpse of a
cockatrice, having removed his ring of levitation by accident.

Slaying Rodney himself was trivial, and with a special ring and a pair
of scrolls, Hi found himself back at the vibrating square.  To his
horror, he found himself to be without candles.  Out came the castle's
wand, and seven candles were suddenly at hand.  Hi performed the
invocation and descended into the Sanctum by scroll, bypassing the
host of undead guardians.  The Bell of Opening revealed the doorway,
and the high priest of Moloch became yet another victim of Hi's zeal.
A cursed potion provided a quick escape from the Sanctum, and the run
to the surface was on.

Rodney appeared once in Gehennom, but was quickly dispatched with
Orcus's wand.  The shallow depth of hell made the trip up seem quick,
but in truth Hi was running as fast as his very fast legs could go.
Reaching the dungeon level just below the surface, Hi paused to
jettison excess weight and to use the second-to-last wish from the
castle wand on another amulet of life saving.  Taking a deep breath,
he climbed the stairs and found himself again next to Rodney.  A blast
of death sent the wizard away once more, and Hi was soon digging his
way to the portal.  On the plane of Air, Rodney once again put in an
appearance but fell just as quickly to the same wand.  The plane of
Fire passed without incident, and on the plane of Water Hi paused only
a moment to vaporize the horde of slithery foes with a single scroll.
Locating the last portal was trivial, and Hi found himself on the
Astral Plane.

Wrapping a towel around his head, Hi found that there were two lich-
kind waiting for him.  They also received a brutal reminder of the
power of scrolls.  The temples were guarded from left to right by
Pestilence, Famine, and Death, and Hi chose to face Pestilence first.
Cutting through the crowd with his athame, Hi laughed as his enemies
fought each other while trying to strike his invisible form.
Pestilence was far out of position and as a result, Hi never had to
face any of the dreaded three riders.  Darting among angels and
priests as though they were statues, Hi made his way towards the
altar.  A vampire lord fleeing from the power of Venus told Hi that he
was in the right place.  With a trill on his magic whistle, Hi
summoned the friendly guardian angel to join with the ranger among the
ranks of the immortals.

